@* One case's conversation, as the back office reads it.

   Extracted so the team queue and the unassigned queue cannot drift: the two render the same transcript for
   the same reader, and a copy is what gets extended in one place and not the other. The customer view is
   deliberately not built on this — it shows a person their own case, with delivery state and read markers
   that would be noise to an agent. *@

@foreach (var message in Messages ?? [])
{
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="0.25rem">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" Gap="0.5rem" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center">
            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption" class="rz-m-0">
                @message.AuthorName — @message.SentAt.ToLocalTime().ToString("g")
            </RadzenText>

            @* Which door it came through, which is not the same question as who wrote it. An entry from a
               channel was attributed on a sender or workspace match rather than by an authenticated caller,
               and an agent deciding how much weight to put on a name needs to see that. Nothing renders for
               a message written here. *@
            @if (message.Source != null)
            {
                <RadzenBadge Text="@message.Source.ToString()" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light" />
            }
        </RadzenStack>
        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2" class="rz-m-0">@message.Body</RadzenText>
    </RadzenStack>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The entries to render, oldest first.</summary>
    [Parameter] public SupportMessage[] Messages { get; set; } = [];
}
